  "before_interfaces": {
    "def-positive-energy-affine-module": [
      "## Definition\n\nLet $\\mathfrak g$ be a finite-dimensional complex simple Lie algebra with the invariant form used in [[def-untwisted-affine-central-extension]]. A representation $\\rho$ of the loop central extension $\\overline{L\\mathfrak g}$ is a **restricted affine-current module of level $k\\in\\mathbb C$** if the central generator acts as $k\\operatorname{id}$ and, for every vector $v$ and current $x\\in\\mathfrak g$, there is an integer $N(v,x)$ such that $\\rho(x\\otimes t^n)v=0$ for all $n\\ge N(v,x)$.\n\nThe algebra in this definition is the central extension only; it does not contain the degree derivation. Restrictedness is a mode-truncation condition and does not itself supply an energy grading. A compatible positive-energy grading is extra structure on this current algebra."
    ],
    "def-witt-algebra": [
      "## Definition\n\nLet $R=\\mathbb C[z,z^{-1}]$ be the algebra of finite Laurent polynomials. Define $\\operatorname{Der}_{\\mathbb C}(R)$ as the vector space of complex-linear maps $D:R\\to R$ satisfying the Leibniz rule $D(fg)=D(f)g+fD(g)$. Let $\\partial_z$ be the linear map with $\\partial_z(z^q)=qz^{q-1}$ for all $q\\in\\mathbb Z$. For each $m\\in\\mathbb Z$, set $d_m=-z^{m+1}\\partial_z$. The **Witt algebra** $W$ is the complex span of the $d_m$ inside $\\operatorname{Der}_{\\mathbb C}(R)$, with bracket the commutator of derivations. The modes are indexed by all integers; all linear combinations in $W$ are finite, and no completion is intended."
    ],
    "lem-adjoint-casimir-is-positive-scalar": [
      "## Statement\n\nLet $\\mathfrak g$ be a finite-dimensional complex simple Lie algebra, let $B$ be the invariant form normalized so long roots have square $2$, and let $\\mathfrak k$ be a compact real form. The adjoint action of the Casimir $\\Omega_B$ from [[def-casimir-operator-relative-to-an-invariant-form]] is a unique positive scalar $\\gamma_B$ times the identity."
    ],
    "def-dual-coxeter-number-for-normalized-form": [
      "## Definition\n\nFor a finite-dimensional complex simple Lie algebra $\\mathfrak g$ as in [[def-loop-algebra-of-a-simple-lie-algebra]], use the invariant form $B$ normalized by long roots of square $2$ in [[def-residue-two-cocycle-on-a-loop-algebra]]. By [[lem-adjoint-casimir-is-positive-scalar]], the Casimir $\\Omega_B$ from [[def-casimir-operator-relative-to-an-invariant-form]] acts in the adjoint representation as $\\gamma_B I$ for a unique positive real scalar $\\gamma_B$. Define the **dual Coxeter number** by $h^\\vee=\\gamma_B/2$. Thus, for a $Q=-B|_{\\mathfrak k}$-orthonormal basis of a compact real form from [[def-compact-real-form-of-a-complex-semisimple-lie-algebra]], $-\\sum_i\\operatorname{ad}(X_i)^2=2h^\\vee I$; this is the normalization used in the affine central term and every Sugawara denominator below."
    ],
    "def-positive-energy-unitary-affine-module": [
      "## Definition\n\nLet $\\mathfrak k$ be the compact real form of the complex simple algebra underlying [[def-positive-energy-affine-module]]. A **positive-energy unitary module** consists of a complex inner-product space (not assumed complete) with positive-definite inner product\n$$H=\\bigoplus_{r\\in\\mathbb Z_{\\ge0}}H_r,$$\nwhere the displayed direct sum is orthogonal. Each $H_r$ is finite-dimensional and $H_0\\ne0$. The representation of the restricted affine-current algebra has central level an integer $k\\ge0$, satisfies $X(n)H_r\\subseteq H_{r-n}$ for every $X\\in\\mathfrak k$ (with $H_s=0$ for $s<0$), and satisfies $X(n)^*=-X(-n)$. In particular zero modes are skew-adjoint on each energy space. This definition selects the nonnegative integral level branch; it does not assert that every positive-energy unitary representation has integral level. The module is **irreducible** if it has no nonzero proper subspace invariant under all current modes.\n\nDefine the energy operator on the graded space by $E|_{H_r}=r\\operatorname{id}$. The stated mode shift gives $[E,X(n)]=-nX(n)$. This is the convention corresponding to $E=-d$ when adjoining the degree derivation $d$ of [[def-degree-derivation-and-full-untwisted-affine-algebra]], which satisfies $[d,x_n]=n x_n$. The derivation $d$ is not part of the current central extension used in the Sugawara mode formula."
    ],
    "lem-sugawara-quadratic-modes-well-defined": [
      "## Statement\n\nLet $\\mathfrak g$ be a finite-dimensional complex simple Lie algebra as in [[def-loop-algebra-of-a-simple-lie-algebra]], with the normalized nondegenerate invariant form $B$ from [[def-residue-two-cocycle-on-a-loop-algebra]]. Let $\\rho$ be a restricted affine-current module of level $k$ as in [[def-positive-energy-affine-module]]. For any $B$-dual bases $(x_a)$ and $(x^a)$, define\n$$Q_m=\\frac12\\sum_a\\sum_{r\\in\\mathbb Z}:J_{x_a}(r)J_{x^a}(m-r):,$$\nwhere $J_x(n)=\\rho(x\\otimes t^n)$ and\n$$:J_x(r)J_y(s):=\\begin{cases}J_x(r)J_y(s),&r<0,\\\\J_y(s)J_x(r),&r\\ge0.\\end{cases}$$\nThen each $Q_m$ is locally finite on every vector of the module and is independent of the chosen dual bases."
    ],
    "lem-witt-central-cocycles-are-cubic": [
      "## Statement\n\nLet $\\lambda:W\\times W\\to\\mathbb C$ be an alternating bilinear central Lie-algebra two-cocycle for the Witt algebra [[def-witt-algebra]], and suppose $\\lambda(d_m,d_n)=0$ whenever $m+n\\ne0$. If $\\lambda(d_1,d_{-1})=0$, then there is a scalar $a\\in\\mathbb C$ such that\n$$\\lambda(d_m,d_n)=a(m^3-m)\\delta_{m+n,0}.$$"
    ],
    "lem-witt-cubic-cocycle-is-a-2-cocycle": [
      "## Statement\n\nFor the Witt algebra of [[def-witt-algebra]], define $\\omega(d_m,d_n)=\\delta_{m+n,0}(m^3-m)/12$ and extend bilinearly. Then $\\omega$ is alternating and satisfies\n$$\\omega([x,y],z)+\\omega([y,z],x)+\\omega([z,x],y)=0$$\nfor all $x,y,z\\in W$."
    ],
    "def-sugawara-modes": [
      "## Definition\n\nLet $\\mathfrak g$ be a finite-dimensional complex simple Lie algebra as in [[def-loop-algebra-of-a-simple-lie-algebra]], with normalized invariant form $B$ from [[def-untwisted-affine-central-extension]]. Let $\\rho$ be a restricted affine-current module of level $k$ as in [[def-positive-energy-affine-module]], and assume $k+h^\\vee\\ne0$ for the number in [[def-dual-coxeter-number-for-normalized-form]]. Choose any $B$-dual bases $(x_a)$ and $(x^a)$ of $\\mathfrak g$. Write $J_x(n)=\\rho(x\\otimes t^n)$.\n\nFor modes, define\n$$:J_{x_a}(r)J_{x^a}(s):=\\begin{cases}J_{x_a}(r)J_{x^a}(s),&r<0,\\\\J_{x^a}(s)J_{x_a}(r),&r\\ge0.\\end{cases}$$\nThe **Sugawara mode** of index $m\\in\\mathbb Z$ is\n$$L_m=\\frac{1}{2(k+h^\\vee)}\\sum_a\\sum_{r\\in\\mathbb Z}:J_{x_a}(r)J_{x^a}(m-r):.$$\nFor the compact real form of [[def-compact-real-form-of-a-complex-semisimple-lie-algebra]], put $Q=-B|_{\\mathfrak k}$; it is positive by the normalized form in [[def-residue-two-cocycle-on-a-loop-algebra]]. If $(X_i)$ is $Q$-orthonormal, then $( -X_i)$ is its $B$-dual, so the same formula reads\n$$L_m=-\\frac{1}{2(k+h^\\vee)}\\sum_i\\sum_{r\\in\\mathbb Z}:J_{X_i}(r)J_{X_i}(m-r):.$$\nBy [[lem-sugawara-quadratic-modes-well-defined]], the mode sum is locally finite on every vector and independent of the chosen dual bases. At the **critical level** $k=-h^\\vee$ the scalar denominator is zero and this normalized formula is not defined; no operator is asserted there."
    ],
    "def-virasoro-algebra": [
      "## Definition\n\nThe **Virasoro algebra** is the vector space $W\\oplus\\mathbb C C$, with $W$ from [[def-witt-algebra]] and $C$ a central basis vector, and bracket\n$$[L_m,L_n]=(m-n)L_{m+n}+\\frac{1}{12}(m^3-m)\\delta_{m+n,0}C,$$\nwhere $L_m$ denotes the lift of $d_m$. The bracket with $C$ is zero. The cocycle identity and alternatingness proved in [[lem-witt-cubic-cocycle-is-a-2-cocycle]] make this central extension a Lie algebra. In a representation, the scalar by which $C$ acts is called the **central charge** $c$; the displayed relation then has $c$ in place of $C$."
    ],
    "lem-irreducible-affine-module-has-irreducible-ground-space": [
      "## Statement\n\nIf $H$ is an irreducible positive-energy unitary module as in [[def-positive-energy-unitary-affine-module]], then its ground space $H_0$ is an irreducible module for the compact zero-mode algebra $\\mathfrak k$."
    ],
    "def-virasoro-highest-weight-module": [
      "## Definition\n\nLet $V$ be a representation of the Virasoro algebra [[def-virasoro-algebra]]. A nonzero vector $v\\in V$ is a **highest-weight vector of weight $h\\in\\mathbb C$ and central charge $c\\in\\mathbb C$** if $L_n v=0$ for every $n>0$, $L_0v=hv$, and $Cv=cv$. The **highest-weight module generated by $v$** is the submodule spanned by all finite words in the Virasoro generators applied to $v$. This definition asserts neither irreducibility nor unitarity; quotienting the generated module by a proper submodule is an additional choice."
    ],
    "lem-sugawara-mode-one-commutator": [
      "## Statement\n\nLet $\\mathfrak k$ be a compact real form of a finite-dimensional complex simple Lie algebra, let $(X_i)$ be orthonormal for $Q=-B|_{\\mathfrak k}$, and let $H$ be a restricted positive-energy unitary affine-current module of level $k\\in\\mathbb Z_{\\ge0}$. For the Sugawara modes in [[def-sugawara-modes]], for every $X\\in\\mathfrak k$ and $m\\in\\mathbb Z$,\n$$[L_m,X(0)]=0,\\qquad [L_m,X(1)]=-X(m+1).$$"
    ],
    "lem-sugawara-commutator-on-all-restricted-modules": [
      "## Statement\n\nLet $V$ be any restricted affine-current module of level $k\\in\\mathbb C$ as in [[def-positive-energy-affine-module]], for a finite-dimensional complex simple $\\mathfrak g$ with normalized invariant form $B$. Put $q=k+h^\\vee\\ne0$ and use [[def-sugawara-modes]]. Then for every $x\\in\\mathfrak g$ and $m,n\\in\\mathbb Z$,\n$$[L_m,J_x(n)]=-nJ_x(m+n).$$\nNo grading, inner product, irreducibility, or integrability of $V$ is required."
    ],
    "lem-sugawara-modes-act-on-currents": [
      "## Statement\n\nLet $V$ be a restricted affine-current module of any complex level $k\\ne-h^\\vee$ as in [[def-positive-energy-affine-module]]. For the modes of [[def-sugawara-modes]], every $x\\in\\mathfrak g$ and $m,n\\in\\mathbb Z$ satisfy\n$$[L_m,J_x(n)]=-nJ_x(m+n).$$\nIn particular this holds on all positive-energy unitary modules in the previously considered nonnegative integral level branch."
    ],
    "thm-sugawara-modes-satisfy-virasoro": [
      "## Statement\n\nLet $\\mathfrak g$ be a finite-dimensional complex simple Lie algebra with invariant form $B$ normalized so long roots have square $2$. On every restricted affine-current module $V$ of complex level $k\\ne-h^\\vee$ as in [[def-positive-energy-affine-module]], the operators of [[def-sugawara-modes]] satisfy\n$$[L_m,L_n]=(m-n)L_{m+n}+\\frac{c}{12}(m^3-m)\\delta_{m+n,0}I_V,\\qquad c=\\frac{k\\dim\\mathfrak g}{k+h^\\vee}.$$\nConsequently these operators and $C\\mapsto cI_V$ define a representation of [[def-virasoro-algebra]]. No energy grading, unitarity, irreducibility or integrability is assumed. The critical level is excluded from this normalized formula."
    ],
